      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tui): reject non-numeric COLORFGBG background values",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `isLightBackground` function parses `COLORFGBG` to detect terminal background color. Some terminals emit values like `\"0;default\"` or `\"0;default;15\"` where `\"default\"` replaces the ANSI color number. `Number.parseInt(\"default\", 10)` returns `NaN`, and `NaN >= 0` is `false`, so the existing code falls through to dark mode — but only by accident, not by design.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd an explicit `/^\\d+$/` check on the raw background value before parsing. This makes the rejection of non-numeric tokens intentional and self-documenting rather than relying on the side effect that `NaN >= 0` is `false`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo behavior change for valid COLORFGBG values. Terminals emitting `\"default\"` continue to fall back to dark mode, but now the intent is explicit.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```text\n$ npx vitest run src/tui/theme/theme.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  24 passed (24)\n```\n\n## AI-assisted\n\nNo.",
